---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Corsarium | About" description="About Corsarium, an open educational platform for structural bioinformatics.">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:py-24">
        <header class="text-center">
            <p class="font-display text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">About</p>
            <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-foreground sm:text-5xl">Corsarium</h1>
        </header>

        <div class="mt-12 space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-foreground-secondary">
            <p class="font-display text-2xl font-medium leading-snug text-foreground sm:text-3xl">
                There is a world we cannot explore directly.
            </p>

            <p>
                Molecules are constantly moving, interacting, and changing at scales far beyond what we can experience ourselves. Yet, through computational methods, we can build a window into this hidden world and begin to explore its dynamics.
            </p>

            <p class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6 font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">
                Corsarium was born from that idea.
            </p>

            <p>
                We see structural bioinformatics and molecular simulation as tools for exploration. They allow us to venture into a world that would otherwise remain invisible to us — to observe molecular systems, understand their behavior, and ask questions about the mechanisms that shape life.
            </p>

            <p>Corsarium is the place where we prepare for those explorations.</p>

            <p>
                It is a community and academy for people who want to learn how to navigate the molecular world. Whether you are taking your very first steps into bioinformatics or looking for new tools and perspectives to expand your existing knowledge, there is a place for you here.
            </p>

            <p>
                Our learning experience is built around <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Voyages</strong>. Each Voyage is a path through a particular area of knowledge, and each one is made up of <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Expeditions</strong> — focused learning experiences designed to help you build the knowledge and skills needed for the journey ahead.
            </p>

            <p>
                We begin with the foundations: understanding where molecular dynamics comes from, learning to work with tools such as NAMD, and becoming comfortable in the Linux environment that supports computational exploration. As Corsarium grows, so will our Voyages, expanding into new tools, methods, and ways of exploring biological systems.
            </p>

            <p>But Corsarium is more than a place to learn.</p>

            <p class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-foreground">It is a community with an identity.</p>

            <p>
                Those who embark on the journey, develop their skills, and reach the level expected within Corsarium become <strong class="font-semibold text-foreground">Corsairs</strong> — members of a community united by curiosity, exploration, and the desire to understand the molecular world.
            </p>
        </div>

        <footer class="mt-16 rounded-2xl border border-border-strong bg-surface-alt px-6 py-12 text-center sm:px-12">
            <p class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-accent-secondary sm:text-3xl">
                Learn. Explore. Become a Corsair.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-foreground-muted">Welcome to Corsarium.</p>
        </footer>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>
